body:
@bmorledge-hampton19 It's likely done for performance reasons. Rotation is not stored separately per particle. Instead, all transformations are contained within the 4x4 transformation matrix that's used for both; 2d and 3d particle. Accumulating rotation would require decomposing the matrix every frame which is relatively costly. 

You can convert particle process material to a shader and look into shader code to see what exactly it is doing. An intervention to that code can be made that decomposes the matrix and accumulates the angle. This will make the curve driven angular velocity behave "as expected".

I've seen people complaining about this on several occasions. This was present even in 4.0 I think. It'd be good to hear directly from developers if performance was indeed the reason for not accumulating. It could be just an oversight though.
